-- Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, Part 7 and Schedule 9 (United Kingdom), edition of 2026-06-30 -- THE SEAT LAYER.   Target: main (checked on build 1.6.109).
--
-- SEAT: a person in or outside the regulated sector who knows or suspects that property is criminal property, or who is asked to deal with it, asking on facts they can state
-- whether they commit an offence under Part 7 or have a defence, and what they must disclose to whom and when.
-- This layer phrases the rules encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask.  Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated here:
-- every question gathers plain answers and calls the layer-1 rule that decides it.  There is no seat for an official (a constable, an NCA officer, a court or the Secretary of State):
-- where a provision addresses only an official, its rule is in layer 1 and the person meets it only through the questions below.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- Where a layer-1 rule expects a record or a MAYBE, it is built inside the question, in its body, from those answers.
--   * A fact the person may not know is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure" (`My answer`); "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * An amount or a day that the person does not know is asked as 0 (or as a yes/no that it exists), and becomes NOTHING.
--   * The orders and regulations that Part 7 points to (the training the Secretary of State specifies, conduct prescribed as unlawful abroad, the excluded businesses, the prescribed form of a disclosure,
--     the regulations on customer due diligence) are not among the sources: the person says whether each applies.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- Never read NOTHING as no.  A result that rests on a reading a lawyer may contest is listed in NOTES.md under "Marginal readings for a lawyer".

DECLARE `My answer` IS ONE OF
    Yes
    No
    `I am not sure`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of Yes, No or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN Yes THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN No THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An amount that the person gives as 0 when they do not know it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`my amount if I know it` MEANS
    IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

-- A day that exists only if the person says it does.
GIVEN `it happened` IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`my day if it happened` MEANS
    IF `it happened` THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An answer about a listed activity of Schedule 9 paragraph 1(1): Yes is what the paragraph lists.  No is the text's no: the Act hands the question to the list
-- ("Schedule 9 has effect for the purpose of determining what is a business in the regulated sector", s 330(12)(a)), so a business in no head is not in the regulated sector.
GIVEN answer IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`what I say about a listed activity` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN Yes THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN No THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping: the Act hands the definition to the list (s 330(12)(a)), so a business in none of its heads is not in the regulated sector
    WHEN `I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An answer about an exclusion of Schedule 9 paragraph 2: an exclusion that applies says the business is NOT in the regulated sector.
GIVEN answer IS A `My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`what I say about an exclusion` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN Yes THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping: the exclusion says "is not in the regulated sector"
    WHEN No THEN NOTHING -- input mapping: an exclusion that does not apply says nothing
    WHEN `I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- A MAYBE BOOLEAN answered by a layer-1 rule, as the BOOLEAN that another layer-1 rule asks for: only JUST TRUE counts.
-- This turns NOTHING into FALSE, which no caller may do with an answer that can be NOTHING.  It is used on four layer-1 answers, each of which is only ever JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE and never NOTHING:
-- s 333C(1) (JUST FALSE for another disclosure, otherwise JUST TRUE), s 339ZK(2), s 339ZD(5) and s 339ZD(4) (each JUST TRUE, otherwise JUST FALSE).  Any other caller is a defect.
GIVEN answer IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`that answer is yes` MEANS
    answer EQUALS JUST TRUE -- input mapping

§ `The Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, Part 7 -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `May I deal with it? The offences of dealing and their exceptions (ss 327 to 329)`
-- Situation: you are about to conceal, transfer, arrange or acquire property you know or suspect is criminal property.  Answer the same facts for each section that fits the act.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Do I commit an offence under section 327 by concealing, disguising, converting, transferring or removing criminal property (s 327(1))?
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Act in section 327(1)` @desc What are you doing with the property?
      `the property is criminal property` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the property criminal property (it is a person's benefit from criminal conduct, or represents one, and you know or suspect that)?
      `I make an authorised disclosure under section 338` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an authorised disclosure under section 338 (see the question on authorised disclosures)?
      `my disclosure is made before I do the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that disclosure made before you do the act?
      `I have the appropriate consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the appropriate consent (see the questions on consent)?
      `I intended to make such a disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to make such a disclosure?
      `I had a reasonable excuse for not making it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse for not making it?
      `my act is done in carrying out a function I have relating to enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act done in carrying out a function you have relating to the enforcement of any provision of this Act or of any other enactment relating to criminal conduct or benefit from criminal conduct?
      `I know, or believe on reasonable grounds, that the criminal conduct occurred outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know, or believe on reasonable grounds, that the criminal conduct occurred in a particular country or territory outside the United Kingdom?
      `the criminal conduct was not unlawful where it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that conduct not, at the time it occurred, unlawful under the criminal law then applying in that country or territory?
      `the criminal conduct is of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that conduct of a description prescribed by an order made by the Secretary of State?
      `I am a deposit-taking body, electronic money institution or payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a deposit-taking body, an electronic money institution or a payment institution?
      `I do the act in operating an account maintained with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do the act in operating an account maintained with you?
      `the value of the criminal property concerned, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the criminal property concerned, in pounds?
      `the threshold amount for my act, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the threshold amount for your act, in pounds (3000 unless a higher amount has been specified; see the question on the threshold amount)?
      `I am carrying on business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you carrying on business in the regulated sector?
      `the business is excluded business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business of a description specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State as excluded business?
      `I do the act in handing over to the customer or client money or other property of, or owing to, the customer or client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do the act in transferring or handing over to a customer or client money or other property of, or owing to, the customer or client (including to another person at their direction)?
      `I do it for the purposes of the termination of my business relationship with the customer or client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that for the purposes of the termination of your business relationship with the customer or client?
      `the total value of the criminal property so handed over, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of the criminal property so transferred or handed over, in pounds?
      `the threshold amount for my termination act, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the threshold amount for your act, in pounds (see the question on the threshold amount for terminating a relationship)?
      `before the act I complied with the customer due diligence duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the act, did you comply with all the customer due diligence duties imposed on you in relation to the customer or client by regulation 28(2), (3), (3A), (4), (8) or (10) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017?
      `I am carrying on business in the regulated sector (mixed funds)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you carrying on business in the regulated sector?
      `I do the act in the course of that business on behalf of a customer or client, in operating an account or holding property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do the act in the course of that business, on behalf of a customer or client, in operating an account or accounts maintained with you or in connection with holding any property for the customer or client?
      `at the time of the act I know or suspect that part but not all of the funds or property is criminal property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act, do you know or suspect that part but not all of the funds in the account or accounts, or of the property so held, is criminal property?
      `it is not possible at the time to identify the part that is criminal property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it not possible, at the time the act takes place, to identify the part of the funds or property that is criminal property?
      `the value of the funds or property after the act, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the funds in the account or accounts, or of the property so held, after the act, in pounds?
      `the value of the criminal property at the time of the act, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of the criminal property at the time of the act, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence under section 327` IS
    `s 327(1) the person commits an offence` (`what I say, as a fact` `the property is criminal property`) `the act` (`Disclosure and exemption facts` OF `I make an authorised disclosure under section 338`, `my disclosure is made before I do the act`, `I have the appropriate consent`, `I intended to make such a disclosure`, `I had a reasonable excuse for not making it`, `my act is done in carrying out a function I have relating to enforcement`, FALSE) (`Overseas conduct facts` OF `I know, or believe on reasonable grounds, that the criminal conduct occurred outside the United Kingdom`, `the criminal conduct was not unlawful where it occurred`, `the criminal conduct is of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State`) (`Account facts` OF `I am a deposit-taking body, electronic money institution or payment institution`, `I do the act in operating an account maintained with me`, `the value of the criminal property concerned, in pounds`, `the threshold amount for my act, in pounds`) (`Termination facts` OF `I am carrying on business in the regulated sector`, `the business is excluded business`, `I do the act in handing over to the customer or client money or other property of, or owing to, the customer or client`, `I do it for the purposes of the termination of my business relationship with the customer or client`, `the total value of the criminal property so handed over, in pounds`, `the threshold amount for my termination act, in pounds`, `before the act I complied with the customer due diligence duties`) (`Mixed funds facts` OF `I am carrying on business in the regulated sector (mixed funds)`, `I do the act in the course of that business on behalf of a customer or client, in operating an account or holding property`, `at the time of the act I know or suspect that part but not all of the funds or property is criminal property`, `it is not possible at the time to identify the part that is criminal property`, `the value of the funds or property after the act, in pounds`, `the value of the criminal property at the time of the act, in pounds`)

@export Do I commit an offence under section 328 by entering into an arrangement that facilitates the use of criminal property (s 328(1))?
GIVEN `I enter into or become concerned in an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you enter into, or become concerned in, an arrangement?
      `I know or suspect that the arrangement facilitates the acquisition, retention, use or control of criminal property by or on behalf of another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know or suspect that the arrangement facilitates (by whatever means) the acquisition, retention, use or control of criminal property by or on behalf of another person?
      `the property is criminal property` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the property criminal property (it is a person's benefit from criminal conduct, or represents one, and you know or suspect that)?
      `I make an authorised disclosure under section 338` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an authorised disclosure under section 338 (see the question on authorised disclosures)?
      `my disclosure is made before I do the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that disclosure made before you do the act?
      `I have the appropriate consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the appropriate consent (see the questions on consent)?
      `I intended to make such a disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to make such a disclosure?
      `I had a reasonable excuse for not making it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse for not making it?
      `my act is done in carrying out a function I have relating to enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act done in carrying out a function you have relating to the enforcement of any provision of this Act or of any other enactment relating to criminal conduct or benefit from criminal conduct?
      `I know, or believe on reasonable grounds, that the criminal conduct occurred outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know, or believe on reasonable grounds, that the criminal conduct occurred in a particular country or territory outside the United Kingdom?
      `the criminal conduct was not unlawful where it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that conduct not, at the time it occurred, unlawful under the criminal law then applying in that country or territory?
      `the criminal conduct is of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that conduct of a description prescribed by an order made by the Secretary of State?
      `I am a deposit-taking body, electronic money institution or payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a deposit-taking body, an electronic money institution or a payment institution?
      `I do the act in operating an account maintained with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do the act in operating an account maintained with you?
      `the value of the criminal property concerned, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the criminal property concerned, in pounds?
      `the threshold amount for my act, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the threshold amount for your act, in pounds (3000 unless a higher amount has been specified; see the question on the threshold amount)?
      `I am carrying on business in the regulated sector` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you carrying on business in the regulated sector?
      `the business is excluded business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business of a description specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State as excluded business?
      `I do the act in handing over to the customer or client money or other property of, or owing to, the customer or client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do the act in transferring or handing over to a customer or client money or other property of, or owing to, the customer or client (including to another person at their direction)?
      `I do it for the purposes of the termination of my business relationship with the customer or client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that for the purposes of the termination of your business relationship with the customer or client?
      `the total value of the criminal property so handed over, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total value of the criminal property so transferred or handed over, in pounds?
      `the threshold amount for my termination act, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the threshold amount for your act, in pounds (see the question on the threshold amount for terminating a relationship)?
      `before the act I complied with the customer due diligence duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Before the act, did you comply with all the customer due diligence duties imposed on you in relation to the customer or client by regulation 28(2), (3), (3A), (4), (8) or (10) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017?
      `I am carrying on business in the regulated sector (mixed funds)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you carrying on business in the regulated sector?
      `I do the act in the course of that business on behalf of a customer or client, in operating an account or holding property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do the act in the course of that business, on behalf of a customer or client, in operating an account or accounts maintained with you or in connection with holding any property for the customer or client?
      `at the time of the act I know or suspect that part but not all of the funds or property is criminal property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time of the act, do you know or suspect that part but not all of the funds in the account or accounts, or of the property so held, is criminal property?
      `it is not possible at the time to identify the part that is criminal property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it not possible, at the time the act takes place, to identify the part of the funds or property that is criminal property?
      `the value of the funds or property after the act, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the funds in the account or accounts, or of the property so held, after the act, in pounds?
      `the value of the criminal property at the time of the act, in pounds` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the value of the criminal property at the time of the act, in pounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence under section 328` IS
    `s 328(1) the person commits an offence` (`what I say, as a fact` `the property is criminal property`) (`s 328(1) the person's act is the act of subsection (1)` `I enter into or become concerned in an arrangement` `I know or suspect that the arrangement facilitates the acquisition, retention, use or control of criminal property by or on behalf of another person`) (`Disclosure and exemption facts` OF `I make an authorised disclosure under section 338`, `my disclosure is made before I do the act`, `I have the appropriate consent`, `I intended to make such a disclosure`, `I had a reasonable excuse for not making it`, `my act is done in carrying out a function I have relating to enforcement`, FALSE) (`Overseas conduct facts` OF `I know, or believe on reasonable grounds, that the criminal conduct occurred outside the United Kingdom`, `the criminal conduct was not unlawful where it occurred`, `the criminal conduct is of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State`) (`Account facts` OF `I am a deposit-taking body, electronic money institution or payment institution`, `I do the act in operating an account maintained with me`, `the value of the criminal property concerned, in pounds`, `the threshold amount for my act, in pounds`) (`Termination facts` OF `I am carrying on business in the regulated sector`, `the business is excluded business`, `I do the act in handing over to the customer or client money or other property of, or owing to, the customer or client`, `I do it for the purposes of the termination of my business relationship with the customer or client`, `the total value of the criminal property so handed over, in pounds`, `the threshold amount for my termination act, in pounds`, `before the act I complied with the customer due diligence duties`) (`Mixed funds facts` OF `I am carrying on business in the regulated sector (mixed funds)`, `I do the act in the course of that business on behalf of a customer or client, in operating an account or holding property`, `at the time of the act I know or suspect that part but not all of the funds or property is criminal property`, `it is not possible at the time to identify the part that is criminal property`, `the value of the funds or property after the act, in pounds`, `the value of the criminal property at the time of the act, in pounds`)

@export Do I commit an offence under section 329 by acquiring, using or possessing criminal property (s 329(1))?
GIVEN `the act` IS A `Act in section 329(1)` @desc What are you doing with the property?
      `the property is criminal property` IS A `My answer` @desc Is the property criminal property (it is a person's benefit from criminal conduct, or represents one, and you know or suspect that)?
      `I make an authorised disclosure under section 338` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make an authorised disclosure under section 338 (see the question on authorised disclosures)?
      `my disclosure is made before I do the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that disclosure made before you do the act?
      `I have the appropriate consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have the appropriate consent (see the questions on consent)?
      `I intended to make such a disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you intend to make such a disclosure?
      `I had a reasonable excuse for not making it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have a reasonable excuse for not making it?
      `my act is done in carrying out a function I have relating to enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your act done in carrying out a function you have relating to the enforcement of any provision of this Act or of any other enactment relating to criminal conduct or benefit from criminal conduct?
      `I acquired, used or had possession of the property for adequate consideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you acquire, use or have possession of the property for adequate consideration (one that is not significantly less than the value of the property or of its use, and not the provision of goods or services you know or suspect may help another carry out criminal conduct)?
      `I know, or believe on reasonable grounds, that the criminal conduct occurred outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you know, or believe on reasonable grounds, that the criminal conduct occurred in a particular country or territory outside the United Kingdom?
      `the criminal conduct was not unlawful where it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that conduct not, at the time it occurred, unlawful under the criminal law then applying in that country or territory?
      `the criminal conduct is of a description prescribed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that conduct of a description prescribed by an order made by the Secretary of State?
      `I am a deposit-taking body, electronic money institution or payment institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a deposit-taking body, an electronic money institution or a payment institution?
      `I do the act in operating an account maintained with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you do the act in operating an account maintained with you?
